{
  "analysis": "I can see the workspace structure with several directories including .claude, .openclaw, output, and skill_context. I need to explore these to understand the safety configuration structure before creating the safety audit report.",
  "plan": "First, I'll explore the workspace to understand the structure - check the skill_context directory for guidance, look at any existing configuration files, and understand what safety-checks, fallback chains, cache data, and session/temp files might exist.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/* 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la output/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la .openclaw/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la .claude/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the SKILL.md file describes the safety-checks skill which requires .openclaw/safety-checks.yaml and .claude/safety-checks.yaml configuration files. I need to explore these directories and check for cache data, session locks, and temp files.",
  "plan": "Continue exploring the workspace - check the .openclaw and .claude directories for config files, look at the output directory, and search for any cache, lock, or temp files in the workspace.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/manifest.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find .openclaw -type f 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat .openclaw/safety-checks.yaml 2>/dev/null || echo 'File not found'\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find .claude -type f 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat .claude/safety-checks.yaml 2>/dev/null || echo 'File not found'\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find . -name '*.lock' -o -name '*temp*' -o -name 'cache*' -o -name '.cache' 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I found the key files for the safety audit:\n- .openclaw/safety-checks.yaml - has model and fallbacks configuration\n- .claude/safety-checks.yaml - has fallbacks configuration\n- .openclaw/cache/staleness.log - cache data to check for staleness\n- .openclaw/safety-checks.lock - session lock file exists\n- ./output/safety/temp-leak-1.log and temp-leak-2.log - potential temp file leakage\n\nI need to check the cache timestamp and create the audit report.",
  "plan": "1. Check the cache staleness log timestamp to determine if it's stale (>1 hour)\n2. Check the lock file details\n3. Create the output/safety directory if needed\n4. Write a comprehensive safety audit report",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la .openclaw/cache/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat .openclaw/cache/staleness.log 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la .openclaw/safety-checks.lock\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la output/safety/ 2>/dev/null || mkdir -p output/safety\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat .openclaw/safety-checks.yaml\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat .claude/safety-checks.yaml\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The safety audit report has been created successfully in output/safety/safety-audit-report.txt. The report covers all required areas:\n1. Safety-checks configuration - verified both YAML files exist\n2. Fallback chain - confirmed model and storage fallbacks are defined\n3. Cache staleness - flagged stale_beta and stale_gamma as exceeding 1-hour TTL\n4. Session lock - noted the lock file presence as a warning\n5. Temp file leakage - identified temp-leak-1.log and temp-leak-2.log\n\nThe report is concise, clear, and notes issues rather than crashing.",
  "plan": "Verify the report file was properly created and check its contents to confirm the task is complete.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la output/safety/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -60 output/safety/safety-audit-report.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
